00380-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Proving and improving the value of consultations</article-title><source>Am J Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>113</volume><fpage>527</fpage><lpage>528</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12427506</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0002-9343(02)01265-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borowsky</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>What do we really know about consultation and referral?</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>497</fpage><lpage>498</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9686720</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1525-1497.1998.00150.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Franks</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Clancy</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Referrals of adult patients from primary care: demographic disparities and their relationship to HMO insurance (health maintenance organization)</article-title><source>J Fam Pract</source><year>1997</year><volume>45</volume><fpage>47</fpage><lpage>53</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9228914</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grimm</surname><given-names>CT</given-names></name><name><surname>Gomez</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of Ambulatory utilization review on referrals from generalists to specialists</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>778</fpage><l